orry we're putting the plug the  light  support machine has been turned off so  this gets to the absolute heart of how  much freedom does the individual have  how much decision-making process to the  parents have or are our children now  owned by the state I mean Nigel what  it's almost like they broke Alfie's  father today because at the beginning of  the day he was saying come here and see  how my son is a hostage of this hospital  which is what we on the show and so many  others have called him he's like a  hostage of the of the National Health  Service and he said what are we what we  are enduring is not right but by the end  of the day he had changed his tune and  basically said everybody go back to your  lives and I think the hospital kind of  sounds like he was threatened and he  said you're not gonna get anything from  us unless you tone it down there was a  picture yesterday of this hospital all  day hey hospital in Northwest of England  with 20 uniformed police officers  standing outside the door of the  hospital to stop little Alfie being  taken out and to stop protesters from  getting in using the police to keep the  child in the hospital now these parents  have been through every single legal  process available to them and I'm  guessing now that the life-support  machine has been turned off now that  there is no prospect at all of the young  boy going to Italy in the end the father  has accepted the inevitable whether he  was threatened or not I don't know but  what I do know is that when I was  involved in this Charlie guard case last  year I turned up outside the hospital in  this case Great Ormond Street Hospital  in London and I was told in no uncertain  terms by the PR services for the  hospital that what I was doing was  damaging the reputation of the hospital  by doing press reports outside where  this little boy was dying and it is just  it's classic of the establishment  closing ranks the state being  all-powerful and frankly what is  happening